		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Undead sea blight formed from the drowning of dozens or hundreds of mortals. Appears as a turgid, grey- black wave filled with ghostly specters.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 10, <strong>HP</strong> 53, <strong>ATK</strong> 2 slam +10 (2d10) and 1 dread gaze, <strong>MV</strong> double near (swim), <strong>S</strong> +6, <strong>D</strong> +0, <strong>C</strong> +4, <strong>I</strong> +0, <strong>W</strong> +2, <strong>Ch</strong> +4, <strong>AL</strong> <strong>C</strong>, <strong>LV</strong> 11</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Capsize</strong>. Opposed STR versus captain's INT or ship is capsized and begins to sink.</p><p></p><p><strong>Dread Gaze</strong>. CHA 15+ or paralyzed 1 round. Each consecutive failure, 1d6 CON damage, death at 0 CON.</p><p></p><p><strong>Greater Undead</strong>. Immune to morale checks. Only damaged by silver or magical sources.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
